Import three PyG utilities from where modern PyG exports them.

ADA-GAD pins torch_geometric==2.2.0, where torch_geometric.utils.degree,
.sort_edge_index and .subgraph were importable submodules. PyG removed those
submodules; the three names are still exported from torch_geometric.utils
itself and are the same functions. Without this the image imports nothing at
all -- the run died at `from main import build_args` with
ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'torch_geometric.utils.degree'.

maybe_num_nodes and torch_geometric.nn.inits are untouched on purpose: both
still resolve at their original paths, so rewriting them would be churn that
could drift.

This changes where three functions are imported from, not what they compute.
Pinning PyG back to 2.2.0 was the alternative and would have dragged torch and
the CUDA build back with it, for the whole image, to avoid three import lines.

Generated with `git diff` against the tree SOURCE_REF pins.

